[Music]  46 years ago martha moxley a 15-year-old  was murdered outside her upscale home in  greenwich connecticut the case made  national headlines and michael skakel a  cousin of the kennedy family was found  guilty of killing her and spent more  than 11 years behind bars but in 2013  his conviction was overturned now  moxley's childhood friends are speaking  out for the very first time they tell  our erin moriarty what they think  happened for this week's 48 hours  on halloween in 1975 in greenwich  connecticut fifteen-year-old martha  moxley was found beaten to death with  the golf club martha's childhood friends  richard burns and tori holland after she  was murdered everything had changed you  have no  sense of peace you've lost it all martha  was last seen with her neighbor 17 year  old tommy skakel the skakels were  cousins of the kennedys tommy's aunt  ethel skakel had married robert kennedy  in 1950. the skakels were also one of  the wealthiest families in the country  yeah that's a famous family they just  had a lot more attitude about you know  they could do anything while tommy was  an early suspect he had an alibi years  went by martha's murder became a cold  case and then in 2002 and 27 years after  the crime  do you have anything to say kennedy  cousin michael skakel convicted in the  murder of martha moxley tommy's younger  brother michael skakel was convicted for  martha's murder  prosecutors concluded that michael was  jealous of his brother tommy's budding  romance with martha but shortly after  michael was convicted robert kennedy jr  told us his cousin had nothing to do  with the murder i know michael skakel  and i know he didn't commit the crime  the evidence is much stronger in  suggesting that other people  may have committed the crime michael  skakel spent almost 12 years in prison  until his conviction was overturned on  appeal and kennedy says evidence  pointing to the real killers can be  found in martha moxley's own diary  and aaron moriarty joins us now erin we  just ended on the diary what do we think  is in this diary well i mean we took a  close look at this diary um like all 15  year olds she kept track of all the guys  that she would see  and investigators do believe that she  knew her killer so what kennedy is  talking about is this dance that she  attended three weeks before she died he  claims that she met a stranger there who  became obsessed with her who then came  back on mischief night and killed her so  we take a look at that entry it is there  we talked to the friends who i mean this  case really mattered and they remember  that night it's not quite the way  kennedy talks about it why is this case  been so hard to solve because it's not  like greenwich is a high crime area no  it's not it's a very small pool of  suspects gail it struck me it wouldn't  happen today think about it all those  houses would have had cameras of course  they would have had cell phone footage  they would have collected you know i  think that greenwich police were just  they weren't equipped for something like  this  all right aaron thank you very much you  can watch aaron's full report the diary  of martha moxley tomorrow night on 48  hours 10 9 central right here on cbs

